## HARD gotchas learned this session (do not rediscover)

- **`prose.cmd` + a shell heredoc in the same Bash call DEADLOCK** — the CLI waits on a stdin the
  heredoc took. Always `< /dev/null`; never put `python - <<'PY'` in the same invocation.
- **Build every prose edit from a fresh dump.** A batch built from a stale dump overwrites newer edits.
- **MCP has its own ambient universe** and `--universe` does not set it. Call `current_universe`
  first; it was stuck on `gutenberg`, making every entity lookup return empty.
- **`create_character` as an update resets `status`→alive and `species`→human when omitted.**
- **Stale inline entity tags are self-perpetuating** — `--tag-entities` returns `Tagged=0` on them;
  only strip-wrapper + `--edit-beat` clears them.
